VOB: keep packed physicsEnabled bit independent of rigid-body payload.

The packed zCVob flag word stores `physicsEnabled` in bit 6 for both Gothic
versions. Its following rigid-body payload is a save-game-only concern, but
the G2 writer incorrectly made bit 6 conditional on a rigid body being
present. Ordinary world VOBs have no such payload, so an enabled flag was
silently cleared during save.

Write the on-disk flag directly. The later `physics_enabled && rigid_body`
payload guard remains unchanged.

diff --git a/src/vobs/VirtualObject.cc b/src/vobs/VirtualObject.cc
--- a/src/vobs/VirtualObject.cc
+++ b/src/vobs/VirtualObject.cc
@@ -278,12 +278,7 @@ namespace zenkit {
 			bit1 |= (!!this->ai) << 4u;
 			bit1 |= (!!this->event_manager) << 5u;
 
-			// Gothic 1 does not store rigid-body information.
-			if (version == GameVersion::GOTHIC_1) {
-				bit1 |= this->physics_enabled << 6u;
-			} else {
-				bit1 |= (this->physics_enabled && this->rigid_body) << 6u;
-			}
+			bit1 |= this->physics_enabled << 6u;
 
 			if (version == GameVersion::GOTHIC_2) {
 				bit1 |= (static_cast<uint8_t>(this->anim_mode) & 3) << 7u;
